  "$comment": "benchmark2 raw-record schema (one JSON object per observation line). Pinned 2026-09-08 (Phase 0). Every record carries settings_hash + kernel_hash + toolchain version from manifest.md. v1.1 (2026-09-11) adds the v2.1 path-class vocabulary and the `spec` record type. That patch IS additive, and this file now says so in a way validate() can honour: required fields are split into `fields` (required of every record) and `fields_since` (required only of records whose `spec_version` names that release). Before 2026-09-15 the v2.1 fields sat in `fields` too, which made every pre-v2.1 record INVALID -- contradicting schema/PATCH-v2.1.md. CHANGED 2026-09-14: the standalone `L` mutation class is FOLDED INTO `M3` (launch/target limits M3.17-M3.26); the mutant/spec `class` enum drops `L`. NON-ADDITIVE: any v1.1 record whose class is `L` must be remapped to `M3`. `path_class` still admits `L` (it is a PATH, not a class). See schema/class-axis.json.",
